Z||000000||PAUL88GT||08-03-2001||01:48 PM||||The letter below is from the leader of the Alabama Fieros Club.  It has hotel information for the 6th Annual Run for the Hills event.  I am not the organizer for this event, but I thought the information may be useful to some of the forum members. I hope to attend myself.<BR>------<BR>Hello Gang,<BR>I'm sorry that this is so late in coming, but it just took longer than I<BR>thought to get the hotel arrangements firmed up. The Sixth Annual Run For<BR>The Hills (RFTH6) is now back on track. We are going to be in some beautiful<BR>Country and we might get a change to see some early fall color. Below is a<BR>very quick note I typed out announcing the RFTH6. It isn't pretty but it<BR>does give the neccessary hotel information. I'll send something out soon<BR>that will be more convincing for the people who haven't had the wonderful<BR>experience of attending a previous RFTH event.<P>Great timing. I just got the hotel information today.<BR>If you need some background info on the RFTH event, here goes...<P>The Run for the Hills is a Fiero driver's dream weekend.<BR>It's a chance to meet with other Fiero owners and spend the weekend driving<BR>on twisty mountain roads. There is nothing better than seeing a long line of<BR>Fieros roaring down the road except for being in that lineup! Everyone with<BR>a Fiero is encouraged to come. There is no show or shine. This is a DRIVER'S<BR>event! We'd rather you have good brakes than good paint.<P>Cherokee, NC is an indian reservation at the foothills of the Great Smoky<BR>Mountains. There are casinos there and souvenir shops. It was also the site<BR>for the Second Annual Run For the Hills.<P><BR>*******************<BR>RFTH6 is going to be in Cherokee, NC. Sept 21-23, 2001.<BR>We may be split up as far as the hotel situation goes if you don't make your<BR>reservations FAST!<P>Main hotel<P>Cherokee Inn (Formerly Econo Lodge)<BR>828-497-2226 ask for JoJo<BR>Rate $55+tax/night<BR>They only have 20 rooms (19 now)  left and there is a Mustang show in town<BR>that weekend. These will probably go FAST!<P>Backup Hotels<P>Pioneer Motel<BR>828-497-2435  (ask for Laurel)<BR>$68+tax/night<BR>They have 18 rooms left<P>Ocona Valley Motel<BR>828-497-4618 (ask for Shirley)<BR>Single bed rooms with Queen $50+tax/night (12 left)<BR>Double rooms  $55+tax/night (only 3 left)<P>In case everything is booked up or you just have extra money to spend...<P>Ramada Limited $85.50+tax night<BR>1-800-489-5263 or 828-497-4231<P>Sleep Inn  $99+tax/night<BR>828-497-4730<P>Smoky Mtn Inn (site of RFTH2)<BR>around $100+tax/night<BR>828-497-2300<P>All of these rooms are on a first come first served basis, and we're<BR>competing with everyone else. Make your reservations soon.<P>More soon.<P>David<BR>||||reg||1
